    "https://easternctstateuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/GCbcnMRgCP/Assistant-Professor-Of-Marketing-And-Management": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Marketing and Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Marketing and Management - Eastern CT State University - Career Page Skip To Job Description View All Jobs View Our Website Eastern CT State University Thanks for visiting our Career Page. Please review our open positions and apply to the positions that match your qualifications. Assistant Professor of Marketing and Management Willimantic, CT Full Time Experienced Share Eastern Connecticut State University Department                       of Business Administration I College of Business Assistant Professor of Marketing and Management Tenure Track I AY 2027- 2028 Eastern Connecticut State University is seeking a qualified candidate to fill the Assistant Professor of Marketing and Management position. Eastern is Connecticut’s Public Liberal Arts University and is located in Willimantic, Connecticut which is 1.5 hours from Boston and 2.5 hours from New York City. Eastern Connecticut State University serves approximately 4,500 students and offers undergraduate majors across the arts and sciences and professional fields, along with select graduate programs. The University is known for small classes, close faculty-student engagement, and a collaborative academic environment. Faculty are supported through professional development, research grants, the Center for Teaching, Learning, and Assessment (CTLA), diversity initiatives, and assistance with external funding for research and educational projects. Eastern is one of four universities in the Connecticut State College and University System (CSCU). The position also offers substantial health and retirement benefits. Position Description: The successful candidate will contribute to a growing Business Administration program while helping develop interdisciplinary opportunities connecting business with entertainment, hospitality, tourism, and related creative industries. The faculty member will be expected to demonstrate excellence in teaching; maintain an active program of scholarly and professional activity appropriate to a tenure-track appointment; advise and mentor students; support undergraduate research and experiential learning; and contribute to departmental, university, professional, and community service. Primary responsibilities will include teaching undergraduate courses in marketing, management, and Eastern's Liberal Arts Core. The successful candidate will also have the opportunity to contribute to the development of proposed curriculum in entertainment management and future interdisciplinary curricular initiatives in entertainment, hospitality, tourism, and related fields. Opportunities may include building partnerships with regional organizations, expanding internship and experiential-learning opportunities, and supporting student professional organizations. Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. or DBA in Marketing, Management, Business Administration, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered; completion of the terminal degree by the time of appointment is required. Evidence of, or strong potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching. Ability to contribute to curriculum development and growth in entertainment, hospitality, tourism, and related fields. Evidence of, or strong potential for, an active scholarly agenda appropriate to the discipline and the expectations of a tenure-track appointment. ​​​​​​​ Commitment to student advising, mentoring, service, and working effectively with students from diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Preferred Qualificati ons: Demonstrated expertise through teaching, research, and/or professional practice in the field of marketing, or closely related sectors. Experience developing applied, interdisciplinary, or career-oriented curricula and programs in entertainment, hospitality, and tourism industries. Meaningful industry engagement and interest in developing external partnerships, internships, and experiential learning opportunities. Potential to contribute to academic and/ or scholarship to the College of Business's ongoing accreditation priorities. Interest in teaching innovative liberal arts core/ELAC seminars that make business concepts accessible to students across disciplines. To Apply : Applicants should submit (1) a letter of interest addressing their qualifications for the position, (2) a current curriculum vitae, and (3) the names and contact information of three professional references through IJAZZHR LINK]. Please submit additional materials only if requested. Applications submitted by November 11, 2026, will receive highest consideration however, the position will remain open until filled. Compensation and Employee Benefits The Assistant Professor of Marketing and Management is compensated at the Assistant Professor salary level in accordance with Connecticut State University American Association of University Professors (CSU-AAUP) Collective Bargaining Unit Agreement. For more information, please visit Bargaining Agreements/Pay Plans - Eastern . The State of Connecticut and Eastern Connecticut State University are proud to offer its employees competitive wages and a wide range of fringe benefits including voluntary and supplemental benefits. Fringe benefits include: paid personal, vacation and sick leave accruals; medical, dental, and prescription plans; group life insurance; retirement; retiree health care; tuition waiver for employee and eligible dependents at any of the Connecticut State Universities (Central, Eastern, Southern or Western) as well as an array of voluntary and supplemental benefits such as Deferred Retirement Contribution plans, Dependent Care Assistance and Medical Flexible spending accounts; long and short term disability insurance plans. For more detailed information, please visit Human Resources - Eastern . Eastern Connecticut State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religious creed, age, gender, gender identity or expression, national origin, marital status, ancestry, present or past history of mental disorder, learning disability or physical disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information or criminal record. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: LaMar Coleman, Ed.D., Vice President for Equity and Diversity. Dr. Coleman can be reached at: 860-465-5112 or via email at: [email protected] . Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file Cover Letter * What's your citizenship / employment eligibility? * No answer I am a U.S. Citizen/Permanent Resident Non-citizen allowed to work for any employer Non-citizen allowed to work for current employer Non-citizen seeking work authorization I am a Canadian Citizen/Permanent Resident Other References: Please enter names and contact information: * Will you have a Ph.D. or DBA in Marketing, Management, Business Administration, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution by date of appointment? * Yes No Can you provide evidence of, or strong potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching? * Yes No Do you have the ability to contribute to curriculum development and growth in entertainment, hospitality, tourism, and related fields? * Yes No Can you provide evidence of, or strong potential for, an active scholarly agenda appropriate to the discipline and the expectations of a tenure-track appointment? * Yes No Are you committed to student advising, mentoring, service, and working effectively with students from diverse backgrounds and perspectives? * Yes No Are you legally authorized to work in the United States? * Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status? (e.g., H-1B visa status) Please note that CSCU does not provide sponsorship * Yes No The following questions are entirely optional. To comply with government Equal Employment Opportunity and/or Affirmative Action reporting regulations, we are requesting (but NOT requiring) that you enter this personal data. This information will not be used in connection with any employment decisions, and will be used solely as permitted by state and federal law. Your voluntary cooperation would be appreciated. Learn more . Gender Decline to answer Female Male Race/Ethnicity Decline to answer Hispanic or Latino White, not Hispanic or Latino Black or African-American, not Hispanic or Latino Asian, not Hispanic or Latino Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander, not Hispanic or Latino American Indian or Alaskan Native, not Hispanic or Latino Two or More Races, not Hispanic or Latino MENA (Middle Eastern and North African) Human Check * Submit Application This website uses cookies and other analytics technologies. By selecting \"Allow\", you consent to the recording, use and sharing of your website activity by this website and its service providers. Allow Reject All Powered by"
