    "https://easternctstateuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/pUCy0Eem8A/Senior-Systems-Software-And-Integration-Engineer": {
      "title": "Senior Systems Software and Integration Engineer",
      "description": "Senior Systems Software and Integration Engineer - Eastern CT State University - Career Page Skip To Job Description View All Jobs View Our Website Eastern CT State University Thanks for visiting our Career Page. Please review our open positions and apply to the positions that match your qualifications. Senior Systems Software and Integration Engineer Willimantic, CT Full Time Experienced Share Senior Systems Software & Integration Engineer Eastern Connecticut State University is seeking a qualified candidate to fill the Senior Systems Software and Integration Engineer position. Eastern is Connecticut’s Public Liberal Arts University and is located in Willimantic, Connecticut which is 1.5 hours from Boston and 2.5 hours from New York City.  Eastern is one of four universities in the Connecticut State College and University System (CSCU). The position also offers substantial health and retirement benefits. Position Summary: Under general supervision, provides technical support and leadership in the areas of information systems administration, problem resolution, system testing, development, integration, and security. Performs and coordinates design, development, testing, deployment, and maintenance of technical solutions to enhance information systems Responsibilities: Develops, maintains, performs and coordinates procedures to ensure integrity of information systems. Leads in design and coordinates with programmers in development of software solutions and integrations. Maintains thorough understanding of software application subsystems, with ability to gauge impact of system access requests and handle items such as code modification and configuration. Performs and coordinates testing, deployment, maintenance of software and database applications and enhancements. Works as a system analyst with key personnel to help define user needs and develop solutions. Coordinates with technical and functional staff to troubleshoot application and database problems. Works with technical and functional staff to analyze, design, construct and implement applications and integrations; help to determine and document business needs and requirements for upgrades and enhancements. Manages moderately complex projects from start to finish, including resource planning. Participates in organization's disaster recovery and business resumption planning, testing, and implementation. Participates in organization's emergency response planning, testing, and implementation. Assists in the implementation of security policies & procedures, along with investigation and resolution of security incidents, to ensure a stable and secure computing environment. Works directly with vendors and technical support personnel on equipment and software purchases, as well as support and maintenance contracts. May supervise professional staff and/or student workers. Performs other duties and responsibilities related to those described above which do not alter the basic level of responsibility of the position. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in computer science, information systems or related field. Advanced degree preferred. Minimum of five (5) years of experience in design, implementation, testing, maintenance, and support of information systems in an ERP environment, preferably Ellucian Banner. Hands on experience with a currently supported version of Oracle RDBMS. Experience with one or more database systems including Microsoft SQL, MySQL, or Postgres is a plus. Certification is a plus. Experience with Unix/Linux operating system in a large-scale, high transactional production environment. Ability to write and debug scripts using common scripting languages like Perl, PHP and Bash. Ability to take ownership and manage small projects from start to completion.​​​​ ​​​​ Excellent customer service and communica1ion skills. Ability to work with people of various backgrounds and on all levels of technical knowledge. Strong organizational, analytical and problem-solving skills. These qualifications may be waived for individuals with appropriate alternate experience. TO APPLY: Applicants should upload a cover letter, current resume and contact information of three professional references to JazzHR at: Senior Systems Software and Integration Engineer - Eastern CT State University - Career Page . Cover letter should be addressed to Chair, Search Committee for the Senior Systems Software and Integration Engineer. Applications submitted by November 13, 2026, will receive highest consideration. Compensation and Employee Benefits The Senior Systems Software and Integration Engineer are compensated at the Administrative V, salary level in accordance with the State University Organization of Administrative Faculty (SUOAF). For more information, please visit Bargaining Agreements/Pay Plans - Eastern . The State of Connecticut and Eastern Connecticut State University are proud to offer its employees competitive wages and a wide range of fringe benefits including voluntary and supplemental benefits. Fringe benefits include: paid personal, vacation and sick leave accruals; medical, dental, and prescription plans; group life insurance; retirement; retiree health care; tuition waiver for employee and eligible dependents at any of the Connecticut State Universities (Central, Eastern, Southern or Western) as well as an array of voluntary and supplemental benefits such as Deferred Retirement Contribution plans, Dependent Care Assistance and Medical Flexible spending accounts; long and short term disability insurance plans. For more detailed information, please visit Human Resources - Eastern . Eastern Connecticut State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religious creed, age, gender, gender identity or expression, national origin, marital status, ancestry, present or past history of mental disorder, learning disability or physical disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, genetic information or criminal record. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: LaMar Coleman, Ed.D., Vice President for Equity and Diversity. Dr. Coleman can be reached at: 860-465-5112 or via email at: colemanla@easternct.edu . Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file Cover Letter * What's your citizenship / employment eligibility? * No answer I am a U.S. Citizen/Permanent Resident Non-citizen allowed to work for any employer Non-citizen allowed to work for current employer Non-citizen seeking work authorization I am a Canadian Citizen/Permanent Resident Other References: Please enter names and contact information: * Do you have a bachelor's degree in computer science, information systems or related field? * Yes No Do you have a minimum of five (5) years of experience in design, implementation, testing, maintenance, and support of information systems in an ERP environment, preferably Ellucian Banner? * Yes No Do you have hands on experience with a currently supported version of Oracle RDBMS. Experience with one or more database systems including Microsoft SQL, MySQL or Postgres? Certification are a plus. * Yes No Do you experience with Unix/Linux operating system in a large-scale, high transactional production environment? * Yes No Do you have the ability to write and debug scripts using common scripting languages like Perl, PHP and Bash? * Yes No Are you legally authorized to work in the United States? * Yes No Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status? (e.g., H-1B visa status) Please note that CSCU does not provide sponsorship * Yes No The following questions are entirely optional. To comply with government Equal Employment Opportunity and/or Affirmative Action reporting regulations, we are requesting (but NOT requiring) that you enter this personal data. This information will not be used in connection with any employment decisions, and will be used solely as permitted by state and federal law. Your voluntary cooperation would be appreciated. Learn more . Gender Decline to answer Female Male Race/Ethnicity Decline to answer Hispanic or Latino White, not Hispanic or Latino Black or African-American, not Hispanic or Latino Asian, not Hispanic or Latino Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander, not Hispanic or Latino American Indian or Alaskan Native, not Hispanic or Latino Two or More Races, not Hispanic or Latino MENA (Middle Eastern and North African) Human Check * Submit Application This website uses cookies and other analytics technologies. By selecting \"Allow\", you consent to the recording, use and sharing of your website activity by this website and its service providers. Allow Reject All Powered by"
